 "status": "ok",
 "readme": "# Drift Simulation with Hidden Contexts\n\nStreaming tabular data synthesis and drift simulation framework used for classification and regression experiments.\n\nThis repository contains:\n- tabular generators (CTGAN, TVAE, CTAB-GAN, TabDDPM, Gaussian Copula, etc.)\n- drift-feature selection (SHAP / Chatterjee)\n- stream construction with abrupt/gradual/incremental/recurrent drift\n- evaluation artifacts and plots used in experiments\n\n## Source Data Included\n\n`House8L`, `WISDM`, `ElecNoreNew`, `superconductivity`\n\n## Environment Setup\n\n```bash\nconda env create -f new_drift_simu.yml\nconda activate new_drift_simu\n```\n\nPython version in the environment file: `3.10.19`.\n\n## Quick Start\n\nRun the test script:\n\n```bash\npython archive/exploratory/test.py\n```\n\n## Outputs\n\nCommon output locations:\n- generated CSVs and drift artifacts: `generated_data/`, `generated_datasets/`, `new_gen_datasets/`\n- checkpoints: `exp_data/`, `saved_generators/`\n- result tables: `results/`, `results_tstr/`, `results_tstr_sklearn/`\n- plots: `plots/`, `stream_plots/`\n\n## Notes\n\n- This project did not provide generator training code, but pre-trained generators are included in `saved_generators/`.\n- Users need to train their own generators if they want to use the code for other datasets.",
